Accept screen streams at any frame rate.

A portal that offers its stream at one fixed rate (COSMIC offers the
display's, e.g. 60/1) has no format in common with a consumer that only
accepts up to the recording frame rate (30 by default): PipeWire fails the
link with "no more output formats".

--- a/crates/isocast-platform-linux/src/pipewire_video.rs
+++ b/crates/isocast-platform-linux/src/pipewire_video.rs
@@ -1389,7 +1389,11 @@
             Fraction,
             Fraction { num: fps, denom: 1 },
             Fraction { num: 0, denom: 1 },
-            Fraction { num: fps, denom: 1 }
+            // The producer's rate, not ours: a compositor that offers one
+            // fixed rate above `fps` (COSMIC: the display's) would otherwise
+            // share no format with us.  The engine takes frames at its own
+            // pace whatever rate they arrive at.
+            Fraction { num: 1000, denom: 1 }
         ),
         property!(
             F::VideoMaxFramerate,
